  "interpretation": "Northern point estimates are positive in the primary and all three prespecified sensitivities, but the frozen northern directional test is unsupported. The primary North-Tropical interaction is near zero and unsupported, and the supplemental-only sensitivity reverses the predicted interaction sign. Independent experimental pollen-limitation data therefore do not recover the proposed context-specific isolation gradient under the frozen model.",
  "claim_ceiling": "This result does not show that pollinators are irrelevant or that islands lack pollen limitation. It shows that the available exact-island GloPL experiments do not support the frozen isolation-associated, North-versus-Tropical pollen-limitation gradient. GloPL is experimental pollen-supplementation evidence, not a direct measure of pollinator abundance decline, visitation decline, historical extinction, or mediation of the Chapter 1 plant-trait response."
